            <ArticleTitle>Primary malignant nerve sheath tumor of the gasserian ganglion: a report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>572-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Primary tumors of the gasserian ganglion are usually benign, and secondary tumors are malignant. We report two cases of a malignant primary tumor of the gasserian ganglion, bringing the total in the world literature to five. The presentation, etiological features, and treatment of these cases are reviewed, together with a review of the literature. Preoperative differentiation from a benign tumor is not possible with certainty. A combination of operation and radiation therapy seems to be the best treatment at present.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
